Show that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is idempotent." 13194139539421 17592186576411 true] [17592186484479 1071 "Source question: Exercise **2.1.24**, [printed page 93 (PDF page 105)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=105).\n\nA matrix is idempotent if $A^2=A$. Show that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is idempotent.\n\nWritten response: {{response}}" 13194139539421 17592186576411 false] [17592186484491 1071 "**(a)** Is $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$ in reduced row-echelon form? Explain." 13194139539421 17592186576411 true] [17592186484491 1071 "**(a)** Is $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$ in reduced row-echelon form? Explain.\n\nWritten response: {{response}}" 13194139539421 17592186576411 false] [17592186484500 1071 "**(d)** Find $CA$ if possible; otherwise explain why it is not defined." 13194139539421 17592186576411 true] [17592186484500 1071 "**(d)** Find $CA$ if possible; otherwise explain why it is not defined.\n\nWritten response: {{response}}" 13194139539421 17592186576411 false] [17592186484501 1071 "Source question: Exercise **1.2.44**, [printed page 47 (PDF page 59)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=59).\n\nA system of linear equations has a unique solution. What must be true of the pivot columns in its augmented matrix?" 13194139539421 17592186576411 true] [17592186484501 1071 "Source question: Exercise **1.2.44**, [printed page 47 (PDF page 59)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=59).\n\nA system of linear equations has a unique solution. What must be true of the pivot columns in its augmented matrix?\n\nWritten response: {{response}}" 13194139539421 17592186576411 false] [17592186484508 1071 "Source question: Exercise **2.1.32**, [printed page 95 (PDF page 107)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=107).\n\nIf $AB=AC$ and $A$ is an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix, must $B=C$? Explain." 13194139539421 17592186576411 true] [17592186484508 1071 "Source question: Exercise **2.1.32**, [printed page 95 (PDF page 107)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=107).\n\nIf $AB=AC$ and $A$ is an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix, must $B=C$? Explain.\n\nWritten response: {{response}}" 13194139539421 17592186576411 false] [17592186484516 1071 "Source question: Exercise **1.2.6**, [printed page 42 (PDF page 54)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=54).\n\nFor the augmented matrix below, $*$ is arbitrary and $\\blacksquare$ is nonzero. Is the system consistent? If so, is its solution unique? Explain.\n\n$$\\left[\\begin{array}{ccccc|c}\\blacksquare&*&*&*&*&*\\\\0&\\blacksquare&*&*&0&*\\\\0&0&\\blacksquare&*&*&*\\\\0&0&0&0&\\blacksquare&*\\end{array}\\right]$$" 13194139539421 17592186576411 true] [17592186484516 1071 "Source question: Exercise **1.2.6**, [printed page 42 (PDF page 54)](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf#page=54).\n\nFor the augmented matrix below, $*$ is arbitrary and $\\blacksquare$ is nonzero. Is the system consistent? If so, is its solution unique? Explain.\n\n$$\\left[\\begin{array}{ccccc|c}\\blacksquare&*&*&*&*&*\\\\0&\\blacksquare&*&*&0&*\\\\0&0&\\blacksquare&*&*&*\\\\0&0&0&0&\\blacksquare&*\\end{array}\\right]$$\n\nWritten response: {{response}}" 13194139539421 17592186576411 false] [17592186484522 1071 "So